The Lean proof rebuilds cleanly, `Proof.final` has the exact fixed type, and Lean reports no axiom dependencies. The operational bridge also passes universal checks for both frozen `valSeqAt` equations and for expansion of every `intVals` sequence; a deliberately shortcut bridge can prove the generated target but fails those checks, while the submitted definition does not. I’m consolidating the evidence and final verdict now.
